%S A394083 0,0,0,0,1,1,1,3,3,4,6,7,9,11,13,15,17,20,22,25,28,31,35
%N A394083 Genus of the n-cycle complement graph.
%C A394083 Euler lower bound gives a(n) >= Ceiling[(n^2 - 9 n + 12)/12].
%C A394083 a(n) equals this bound for n = 0 or 9 (mod 12).
%C A394083 It is conjectured that a(n) = ceiling((n^2 - 9*n + 12)/12) for all n >= 8 except a(10) = 3. - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Jul 25 2026
%C A394083 The values a(21)-a(25) were obtained by exact genus computation or from the equality cases above, with embedding certificates attaining the Euler lower bound for the computed cases. - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Jul 25 2026
%C A394083 Since the complement of the (n+1)-wheel graph is the disjoint union of an isolated vertex and the n-cycle complement graph, its genus is a(n). - _Eric W. Weisstein_, Jul 25 2026
